<Guide slug="shoulder-season" photo="dubrovnik">
  <p>
    Shoulder season is the period just before and after a destination’s peak season. The weather is often nearly as good,
    but crowds are thinner, hotels are cheaper and locals are more relaxed. For many places it’s simply the best time to go.
  </p>
  <p>
    There’s no single shoulder season: it depends on when a destination’s peak is. Below are the shoulder months for the main
    travel regions, with our weather ratings so you can see how little you give up.
  </p>

  <h2>Europe: April–May and September–October</h2>
  <p>
    Southern Europe’s summer peak (July–August) brings heat, crowds and the highest prices. In late spring and early autumn,
    it’s warm enough to sightsee all day — and in September and early October the sea is still warm enough to swim.
  </p>
  <GuideTable caption="European destinations in shoulder season" months={[3, 4, 8, 9]} rows={[{ slug: 'rome' }, { slug: 'barcelona' }, { slug: 'lisbon' }, { slug: 'santorini' }, { slug: 'dubrovnik' }, { slug: 'amalfi-coast' }, { slug: 'provence' }, { slug: 'paris' }]} />

  <h2>The Caribbean and Mexico: late April–June and November–mid-December</h2>
  <p>
    The dry high season runs from mid-December to mid-April. Late April to June is still mostly dry and sunny, while November and
    early December follow the end of hurricane season — both with noticeably lower resort prices.
  </p>
  <GuideTable caption="Caribbean destinations in shoulder season" months={[4, 5, 10, 11]} rows={[{ slug: 'aruba' }, { slug: 'punta-cana' }, { slug: 'jamaica' }, { slug: 'barbados' }, { slug: 'cancun' }, { slug: 'turks-and-caicos' }]} />

  <h2>Southeast Asia: November and March–April</h2>
  <p>
    Thailand, Vietnam and Cambodia peak from December to February. November is often fresh and green after the rains, while March
    and April are hot but less busy (and Songkran, Thai New Year, falls in mid-April).
  </p>
  <GuideTable caption="Southeast Asian destinations in shoulder season" months={[2, 3, 10]} rows={[{ slug: 'bangkok' }, { slug: 'chiang-mai' }, { slug: 'hanoi' }, { slug: 'siem-reap' }, { slug: 'phuket' }]} />

  <h2>US national parks: May and September–October</h2>
  <p>
    Summer brings school-holiday crowds and desert heat. May and early autumn have open roads in most parks, cooler hiking
    temperatures and fewer people — and golden aspens or fall colours in late September and October.
  </p>
  <GuideTable caption="US national parks in shoulder season" months={[4, 8, 9]} rows={[{ slug: 'zion' }, { slug: 'grand-canyon' }, { slug: 'yellowstone' }, { slug: 'arches-bryce' }, { slug: 'acadia' }]} />

  <h2>Japan: mid-April to May and October to mid-November</h2>
  <p>
    Cherry blossom season (late March–early April) and peak autumn colours (late November) are the busiest. The weeks around them
    are mild and beautiful — just avoid Golden Week in early May.
  </p>
  <GuideTable caption="Japan in shoulder season" months={[3, 4, 9, 10]} rows={[{ slug: 'tokyo' }, { slug: 'kyoto' }, { slug: 'osaka' }, { slug: 'hokkaido' }]} />

  <h2>How to make the most of shoulder season</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Avoid holiday weeks</b> — Easter, half-terms and national holidays can make a shoulder week feel like peak season.</li>
    <li><b>Check what’s open:</b> on some islands (the Greek islands, Ibiza, the Amalfi Coast), hotels and ferries only start running fully from May.</li>
    <li><b>Pack a layer</b> for cooler evenings.</li>
    <li><b>Book flexible rates,</b> as spring and autumn weather can be more variable.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Browse every month: <a href="/calendar/">the travel calendar</a>.</p>
</Guide>
